<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dhaka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dhaka is the capital and largest city of Bangladesh, on the Buriganga river in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> delta. Made the Mughal capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a> by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> Khan in 1610, it flourished on the muslin trade, and later became the capital of the province of Eastern Bengal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> from 1905 to 1911, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-pakistan">East Pakistan</a>, and from 1971 of independent Bangladesh. It is one of the most densely populated cities in the world.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dhaka.jpg" alt="Dhaka" width="320" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Meer Sadi · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Downtown_Hatirjheel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
